\section{Experiment}

\paragraph{Implementation Detail.} We train the grounding models using dataset collections from Aria-UI \cite{yang2024aria} and OS-Atlas \cite{wu2024atlas}, applying a data cleaning threshold of $\tau = 0.3$. Our model is initialized from UI-TARS-1.5-7B \cite{qin2025ui}, Qwen2.5-VL-32B-Instruct \cite{bai2025qwen2}, and Qwen2.5-VL-72B-Instruct \cite{bai2025qwen2}. We use a learning rate of $10^{-6}$ and sample $N = 8$ responses per input during training. The batch sizes are set to 256, 128, and 128 for the 7B, 32B, and 72B models, respectively. The 7B and 32B models usually converge around 250 iterations, while the 72B model converges around 50 iterations. When testing on the real-world dynamic environment, we use the action space from \cite{agashe2025agent} and o3 as the planner \cite{openAI_o3_o4_mini}.

\paragraph{Dataset.} We evaluate our method on two sets of benchmarks: i) GUI Grounding: we use ScreenSpot-V2 \cite{cheng2024seeclick,wu2024atlas}, ScreenSpotPro \cite{li2025screenspotpro}, and OSWorld-G \cite{xie2024osworld} datasets, evaluating using the metric of accuracy; ii) Agent Task Execution: we use OSWorld \cite{xie2024osworld} benchmark, measuring performance by task success rate.

\paragraph{Baseline.} We compare with various state-of-the-art methods: CogAgent \cite{hong2024cogagent}, OminiParser \cite{lu2024omniparser}, 
Qwen2.5-VL \cite{bai2025qwen2}, Aria-UI \cite{yang2024aria}, OS-Atlas \cite{wu2024atlas}, UGround \cite{gou2024navigating}, ShowUI \cite{lin2025showui},  Aguvis \cite{xu2024aguvis}, Jedi \cite{xie2025scaling}, GUI-G1 \cite{zhou2025gui}, SE-GUI \cite{yuan2025enhancing}, GUI-R1 \cite{luo2025gui}, UI-R1 \cite{lu2025ui}, InfiGUI-R1 \cite{liu2025infigui}, UI-TARS \cite{qin2025ui}, Seed-1.5-VL \cite{guo2025seed1}, UI-TARS-1.5 \cite{qin2025ui}, GPT-4o \cite{hurst2024gpt}, o3 \cite{openAI_o3_o4_mini}, Claude 3.7 Sonnet \cite{claude37}, and Gemini-2.5 \cite{gemini25}.


