\section{Conclusions}
We developed a comprehensive database of 7,123 thermoelectric compounds, incorporating key thermoelectric and structural properties using the automated data extraction capabilities of the GPTArticleExtractor. By including structural information, our database is well-suited for future use with advanced methods such as graph neural networks, enabling predictive modeling and material analysis. The database is openly accessible at \href{http://nemad.org}{nemad.org} and is continually updated and expanded. This work provides a valuable resource for data-driven research in sustainable energy, supporting the discovery and analysis of thermoelectric materials and contributing to advancements in the field.







