\section{\large The unitary relationship between tensor product operators}\label{se:unitary}

\skp{-1}
In this section we examine
the relationship between two tensor product operators.  
Within a type $\mathcal{H}_1 \cross \mathcal{H}_2 \longrightarrow \mathcal{H}$, the relationship between two tensor product operators $\otimes_1$ and $\otimes_2$ is given by a uniquely determined unitary operator $U_{\otimes_1,\otimes_2}$ on the target space of the type.  $U_{\otimes_1,\otimes_2}$ is given in terms of the action of the two tensor product operators on the bases of $\mathcal{H}_1$ and $\mathcal{H}_2$.
