The operator pairs $\otimes_{(13)2}$ and $\otimes_2$, $\otimes_{1(23)}$ and $\otimes_1$, and 
$\otimes_{(12)3}$ and $\otimes_3$ satisfy what we normally \textit{and informally} write as the right side of each of
\begin{equation}\label{def:t-OpPairs}
\begin{array}{l}
(\ket{i}_{{\sf A}_1} \otimes_2 \ket{k}_{\sf B}) \otimes_{(13)2} \ket{j}_{{\sf A}_2} = \ket{i}_{{\sf A}_1} \otimes_1 \ket{j}_{{\sf A}_2} \otimes_1 \ket{k}_{\sf B}\,, \\
\rule{0pt}{3ex}\ket{i}_{{\sf A}_1} \otimes_{1(23)} (\ket{j}_{{\sf A}_2} \otimes_1 \ket{k}_{\sf B}) = \ket{i}_{{\sf A}_1} \otimes_1 \ket{j}_{{\sf A}_2} \otimes_1 \ket{k}_{\sf B}\,, \\
