\begin{Lemma}\label{le:Asmbly} {\em Let $\mathcal{H}_1$ and $\mathcal{H}_2$ be finite dimensional Hilbert spaces and let 
$\{\ket{e_i} \mid i = 0,\ldots,m-1\}$ and $\{\ket{f_j} \mid j = 0,\ldots,n-1\}$ 
be ordered orthonormal bases.  Let $\mathcal{H}$ be a Hilbert space with ordered orthonormal basis $\{\ket{h_\lambda} \mid \lambda = 0,\ldots,mn-1\}$.  Then there exists a tensor product operator $\otimes: \mathcal{H}_1 \cross \mathcal{H}_2 \longrightarrow \mathcal{H}$
such that $\ket{e_i} \otimes \ket{f_j} = \ket{h_{ni+j}}$.
}
\end{Lemma}
\textit{Proof}: $\otimes$ is the bilinear extension of the lexicographic order-preserving bijective function 
from $\{\ket{e_i} \mid i = 0,\ldots,m-1\} \cross \{\ket{f_j} \mid j = 0,\ldots,n-1\}$ 
to 
$\{h_{ni+j} \mid i = 0,\ldots,m-1,\ j = 0,\ldots,n-1\}$, 
which is $\{h_\lambda \mid \lambda = 0,\ldots,mn-1\}$ in the same order. 
$\hspace*{\fill}\QED$
