\end{equation}
Therefore the {\sf CNOT} gate in the circuit between locations 2 and 3 must implement the {\sf NOT} with respect to $\otimes_3$.   Also note, counterfactually,  that if it were possible to change the tensor product operation between states of ${\sf A}_2$ and ${\sf B}$ to $\otimes_1$ from $\otimes_3$, the first {\sf CNOT} gate would not be needed.

