\subsection{Package and Bonding}
As a package, a Very thin Quad Flat No leads package (VQFN) with a ground connection at the bottom of the package is chosen. The chip fits well into larger variants, which means that the longest bonding wires should not exceed \SIrange{2.5}{3}{mm}, limiting the wire inductivity and making high data bandwidths possible. The substrate is glued on the island, providing a very good ground connection and low thermal resistance. The ground pads of the chip are connected with down-bonds to the package bottom. 
