The task can be categorized into the following three independent dimensions:


\noindent \textbf{Question types.} Two primary question types are engaged.
1) \textbf{Yes-or-No}: To address potential affirmative bias in MLLMs, the ratio of answers is balanced to approximately $1:1$ \cite{Q-bench-video}, ensuring the objectivity of the evaluation.
2) \textbf{What/How}: Designed to capture nuanced emotional perception, emphasizing more precise perception capabilities. While \textit{what} questions focus on identifying specific emotions and their causes, \textit{how} questions assess the perception of emotional properties, especially VAD attributes. 

