(\textit{The analysis of the four dimensions, segmented by question concerns, is provided in Supp. \ref{supp: extended results}.})

2) Perceptual dimensions.
Further analysis from Tab. \ref{tab: perception} reveals that MLLMs effectively recognize salient emotional features, such as valence that derived from colors and representative objects. However, their understanding remains insufficient for more nuanced emotional attributes, like dominance and arousal, that require a deeper integration of human common sense and subjective preferences. This underscores the need to enhance MLLMs' systematic capabilities regarding emotions evoked by images. (\textit{We further illustrate our findings on $6$ content categories in Supp. \ref{supp: extended results}}.)



