To estimate orders of magnitude, we measure memory consumption for a \SI{2}{\hertz} simulation of our test model, with 64 sources. This leads to around 20 million complex-valued unknowns. Since the LUMI cluster has nodes with \SI{256}{\giga\byte} and 128 cores, we aim for a partitioning where each subdomain can be solved on a single-thread process and less than \SI{2}{\giga\byte}. We partition into either 256, 512, or 1024 subdomains and run the simulations accordingly.

