A common technique to measure packet loss in the Internet is through the use of \emph{sequence numbers} (e.g., in the RTP protocol~\cite{schulzrinne2003rfc}).
The sequence number is incremented for each data packet sent, allowing the receiver to detect packets that do not arrive.
We apply a similar approach (referred to as the sequence method) to measure data loss, which we describe in Section \ref{subs:sequence_method}.
