Standard YOLO loss functions for objectness, classification, and bounding box regression are applied. All configurations were trained for  500 epochs, with the best checkpoint (all reached before the final epoch) selected for testing.

\subsection{Advantages of the Proposed Approach}

Our method offers:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Simplicity:} Only minor changes to existing models.
    \item \textbf{Efficiency:} Minimal overhead in parameters and computation.
    % \item \textbf{Scalability:} Compatible with lightweight or heavyweight detectors.
    \item \textbf{Sparse supervision:} Only one frame per stack needs to be labeled.
\end{itemize}

We demonstrate in experiments that this approach improves detection robustness, particularly in challenging scenes with occlusions and motion artifacts.



