The evolution of operating systems (OS) has been shaped by the continuous interplay between technological advancements and the changing demands of computing environments. From the early days of manually configured systems to today’s sophisticated platforms, OS development has been driven by the need to efficiently manage resources, enhance usability, and adapt to emerging paradigms. Key milestones, such as the introduction of Unix and the rise of graphical user interfaces, laid the foundation for modern operating systems, enabling multitasking, modularity, and accessibility. Over the decades, the diversification of computing devices, from desktops and mobile devices to embedded systems, has further propelled innovations in OS design to address the unique requirements of specialized hardware and applications.

In recent years, the integration of artificial intelligence (AI) into operating systems has emerged as a transformative trend, unlocking new opportunities for intelligent resource management, adaptive performance, and enhanced user experiences. AI encompasses a range of technologies, including expert systems, machine learning (ML), and large language models (LLMs), each contributing distinct capabilities to OS functionality. By embedding AI technologies, operating systems can evolve from static, rule-based platforms into dynamic, intelligent systems capable of optimizing operations, predicting user needs, and addressing the growing complexity of modern computing environments.

The motivation for integrating AI into OS lies in its potential to address critical challenges in areas such as resource allocation, security, and system adaptability. For example, ML algorithms enable OSs to learn from data and adjust configurations dynamically, while LLMs enhance user interactions through natural language processing, enabling intuitive and conversational interfaces. Additionally, the adoption of AI-driven techniques aligns with emerging trends in computing, such as the Internet of Things (IoT), edge computing, and cloud systems, where managing large-scale, interconnected environments requires intelligent and scalable solutions.


This survey explores the intersection of AI and OS, providing a comprehensive review of recent advancements, challenges, and future opportunities. We categorize the integration of AI technologies into two key aspects of OS development: design and operational optimization. Our analysis is based on an extensive review of primary studies, highlighting the impact of AI on OS performance, efficiency, and adaptability. The remainder of this paper is organized as follows: Section 2 outlines the scope and objectives of the survey. Sections 3 and 4 discuss AI-driven methodologies for OS development and operational enhancements. Section 5 examines the integration of LLMs into OS architectures, and section 6 discusses the clarification of different stages of AI-assisted OSs. Section 7 identifies emerging trends and future directions, while Section 8 concludes the paper, summarizing the key insights and contributions.

Here are the highlights of this paper:
\begin{itemize}
    \item We identify and discuss the application of ML tools across various subdomains of operating systems. 
    % We examine how AI techniques are being applied to improve core functionalities such as memory management and process scheduling.
    \item We provide detailed insights into a variety of ML algorithms used in different areas of operating system research, which includes understanding the specific methodologies employed to achieve performance improvements and security enhancements.
    \item We explore how LLMs can be utilized within the context of operating systems, suggesting new research avenues and potential improvements that can be realized through their integration.
    \item We identify novel operating system architectures that provide opportunities for the development of intelligent operating systems. This includes examining designs that facilitate better AI integration and enable advanced features such as dynamic resource allocation and improved security protocols.
    \item We define and outline the different stages of AI integration within operating systems, providing a roadmap for ongoing and future research efforts aimed at enhancing OS functionality through AI.
\end{itemize}

