\section{Related Search}
Previous research has made significant strides in exploring the integration of AI with OS \cite{zhang2019learned}. For instance, \cite{agarwal2023artificial} examines the application of quantum computing in cybersecurity, highlighting how AI and qubit-based operating systems can enhance security measures. This work points to the potential of quantum-enhanced systems to effectively address complex security challenges. Additionally, \cite{wohlrabapplication} investigates the use of object-oriented programming and AI methodologies to structure and optimize operating systems, advocating for more compact, customized systems that meet the diverse and evolving demands of various computing environments. This study underscores the importance of adaptability and efficiency in modern OS design. In \cite{korshun2023automation}, the focus is on the role of AI and ML in OS management, presenting a framework for their integration aimed at enhancing resource allocation, security, performance, and system adaptability. This research emphasizes the need for intelligent systems capable of self-optimization and dynamic responses to changing conditions. Furthermore, \cite{ranasinghe2009artificial} assesses the impact of various AI techniques on key aspects of distributed operating systems, including resource management, fault tolerance, and security. \cite{safarzadeh2021artificial} focuses on the improvements that ML can bring to OS resource management, while \cite{sibai2023}, \cite{qiu2020survey}, and \cite{sk2022literature} address security aspects of operating systems. Additionally, \cite{pereira2021learning} explores the application of AI methods in software configurations.

While these works have provided valuable insights and advancements, they often concentrate on specific types of operating systems or may now be considered somewhat outdated, particularly given the recent emergence and rapid development of large language models \cite{zhao2023survey}. As we move forward, it will be crucial to explore how LLMs and other cutting-edge AI technologies can be integrated into operating systems to drive the next wave of innovation in computing.

