Evaluation of a code generated by LLM is challenging, as LLMs are usually trained to write code for object-oriented programming languages like C/C++ and Python, which are usually not time-dependent and do not generate combinational and sequential logic. Our criteria to evaluate SystemVerilog code are on 3 three-prong basis to completely evaluate and accept the generated code as working. The criteria in the order are as follows:

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Lint Check}: We use the industry standard Synopsys Spyglass Fault Analyzer. This is the first step, which looks for any syntactical or logical errors generated by the code.

