\textbf{Example 2:} Consider LoD adaptation of point clouds. The uniformity of the explicit representation provided by point clouds, static or dynamic, considerably simplifies LoD adaptation~\cite{vivo,GROOT20}. Storing the points in 3D hierarchical space partitioning schemes, such as octrees \textcolor{black}{(where each internal node has exactly eight children)} or kd-trees \textcolor{black}{(binary trees where every node is a k-dimensional point)}, provides the LoDs needed for specific viewing distances, network conditions, cache configurations, or client rendering capabilities.
For example, Figure~\ref{fig:ptcloud} illustrates progressive refinement when rendering a point cloud with a coarse LoD (left) to a fine LoD (right). 

