%(3) For a subtree $T^i_v$ rooted at a child of $v$ in $T$, if there exists a vertex of $T^i_v$ adjacent of $u$ in $G\setminus {v}$, the $T^i_v$ becomes a subtree rooted at a child of $u$ in $T'$; otherwise $T^i_v$ remains rooted at $v$ in $T'$.

